Workstream ID: mission-clarity
Title: Make mission checkpoints distinct and explain the hierarchy interactively
Status: DONE
Milestone: An action-first mission page and a clear animated progression example
Dependencies: tracker-foundation, tutorial-and-help
GitHub issue: https://github.com/Zanark/CareerOS/issues/30
Purpose: Make the current checkpoint visually distinct, remove repeated
  stage/checkpoint names and clarify primary priority versus in-focus planning.
  Move recorded work into one compact card with contextual counting help and
  move Operation documents to the bottom. Add a polished, optional Missions
  walkthrough with multiple example missions and checkpoints. Keep saved work,
  completion rules, source adoption and the previous local refinements intact.

Tasks:
  [x] Trace mission rendering, planning priority and explicit completion rules.
  [x] Compact the streak and preserve its tutorial/contextual-help behavior.
  [x] Restyle the checkpoint and move documents below the mission content.
  [x] Add the animated mission/stage/checkpoint/evidence walkthrough.
  [x] Qualify accessible controls, motion, layout and real progression guards.
  [x] Update focused documentation, original tracking and owned continuity.
  [x] Prepare the preserved current-source preview for local review.

Acceptance criteria:
  The current checkpoint has a flag/number, unambiguous checkpoint title,
    separate stage metadata, actual mission progress and next unlock.
    A stage matching its checkpoint name is not repeated as another title.
  Recorded streak is a compact secondary card, not a full-width introductory
    row. Actual recorded-day status remains; counting moves to existing
    click/tap/hover/keyboard contextual help and the tutorial remains usable.
  Operation documents is last on the mission page. Adoption confirmations,
    material warnings, version information and all existing links remain.
  Primary is the single planning priority, not activation or completion.
    Only eligible in-focus missions enter a newly generated capacity-bound plan.
  Missions has an inviting button opening a readable, polished native dialog.
    Its fictional multi-mission example shows stages, multiple checkpoints,
    saving evidence versus criteria-confirmed completion, next unlock and
    mission completion without automatically completing another mission.
  Animation is bounded, pausable/replayable and manually navigable. Reduced
    motion, hidden tabs, closing/unmount, focus return and narrow screens work.
    The example is not real progress and cannot call workspace writers.
  Both themes retain readable type and meaningful icons; no external media,
    new dependencies, workspace/schema changes or invented mastery.
  Preserve prior calendar/blocker/playlist work, real browser data and the
    illustrated README. No image inspection or unauthorized publication;
    later shipping authority and proof are recorded separately in workstream32.
  Technical evidence, human design review and publication remain separate.

